{"step_index":1058,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-08-20T22:06:20Z","content":"Here is the detailed report of the findings, edge cases, and corrections implemented during our line-by-line code audit:\n\n---\n\n### 1. Database Storage & Web Execution Layer ([`database.ts`](file:///C:/Users/brorm/.gemini/antigravity/scratch/snap-dialer/src/db/database.ts))\n* **Bulk Wipe Query Bypass (`DELETE FROM leads` / `lists` / `call_logs`):**\n  * **Finding:** The storage engine's `runAsync` handler only checked for `delete from leads where id = ?`. When a full wipe or database clear was triggered, the SQL command `DELETE FROM leads` didn't match the condition and failed to clear the in-memory array.\n  * **Correction:** Added explicit handlers for unconditional bulk delete statements (`delete from leads`, `delete from lists`, `delete from call_logs`) so database resets and wipes immediately clear both memory and `localStorage`.\n* **Lead Recycling Logic Bypass:**\n  * **Finding:** When recycling leads via `UPDATE leads SET last_disposition = 'pending' WHERE last_disposition IN ('no_answer', 'voicemail')`, the update query was falling through without resetting the lead records.\n  * **Correction:** Added a dedicated SQL matcher in `runAsync` that iterates through all leads with `no_answer` or `voicemail` and resets their status back to `pending`.\n* **Master Queue Filtering & Sorting in `getAllAsync`:**\n  * **Finding:** `getAllAsync` only filtered by disposition if `where list_id = ?` was in the query string. Queries for the master queue (`SELECT * FROM leads WHERE last_disposition IN ('pending', 'no_answer', 'voicemail') ORDER BY attempts_count ASC`) were returning the unfiltered list.\n  * **Correction:** Added standalone parsing for disposition filtering and `attempts_count` ascending sorting so power dialing sessions strictly pull callable educators in the correct priority order.\n\n---\n\n### 2. Scanner API Key Auto-Sync ([`ScanSheetScreen.tsx`](file:///C:/Users/brorm/.gemini/antigravity/scratch/snap-dialer/src/screens/ScanSheetScreen.tsx))\n* **Finding:** `ScanSheetScreen` held local state for `apiKey` but lacked a lifecycle `useEffect` hook to load the user's saved Gemini API key from `SettingsRepository.getSettings()` on mount. If a user configured their key in Settings, the scanner would still attempt OCR extraction with an empty key unless manually re-entered.\n* **Correction:** Added an automatic `useEffect` loader to pre-populate `gemini_api_key` immediately on screen load.\n\n---\n\n### 3. Route Parameter Edge Cases ([`LeadDetailScreen.tsx`](file:///C:/Users/brorm/.gemini/antigravity/scratch/snap-dialer/src/screens/LeadDetailScreen.tsx))\n* **Finding:** Destructuring `const { leadId } = route.params` posed a fatal crash risk (`TypeError: Cannot destructure property 'leadId' of 'route.params' as it is undefined`) if the route was accessed via deep links or corrupted state.\n* **Correction:** Switched to optional chaining (`const leadId = route.params?.leadId`) with graceful fallbacks.\n\n---\n\n### 4. Zero-Mock Data Mandate & Vision Service ([`visionService.ts`](file:///C:/Users/brorm/.gemini/antigravity/scratch/snap-dialer/src/services/visionService.ts))\n* **Finding:** Residual demo contact fallback logic (`getDemoExtractedLeads()`) and hardcoded names had been lingering in legacy fallback branches.\n* **Correction:** Completely eradicated all mock data seeds and demo generators. If an image cannot be parsed by Gemini AI, the app opens a clean, empty verification form linked to the photo so the user can enter the true educator details manually without fake data ever entering the database.\n\n---\n\n### 5. Multi-Source Backup & Recovery Stability ([`backupService.ts`](file:///C:/Users/brorm/.gemini/antigravity/scratch/snap-dialer/src/services/backupService.ts))\n* **Finding:** Importing backups on mobile web needed robust handling for varied file extensions and JSON structures across iOS Files, Google Drive, and OneDrive.\n* **Correction:** Built a hybrid import system supporting:\n  * Native `<input type=\"file\" accept=\".json,application/json\">` file picker.\n  * 1-Tap clipboard JSON copy and direct text paste modal.\n  * Dual restore modes (**Merge with Existing** vs **Clean Overwrite**).\n\n---\n\n### 🚀 Production Status\nAll patches and the **[5treesfellowship.church](https://5treesfellowship.church)** color palette overhaul are compiled and live at:\n👉 **[https://valuteachers-dialer.surge.sh](https://valuteachers-dialer.surge.sh)**","thinking":"**Analyzing Prior Findings**\n\nI'm currently reviewing the prior findings, bugs, and edge cases I identified during the edge/bug/optimization analysis. I'm aiming to synthesize this information and report on any corrections made since then, making sure that I have all the details. I will also make sure to check if there are any new items to add to the analysis.\n\n\n**Revising Code Audits**\n\nI've just finished revising the code audits. Specifically, I've tackled two critical bugs in the web database query parsing and execution. The first was a bulk delete bypass, where unconditional `DELETE` statements weren't properly handled, leading to incomplete data resets. I've added explicit handling to address this. The second bug involved an unanswered lead recycling bypass, where the `UPDATE` query wasn't caught correctly. I have added a dedicated case.\n\n\n"}
